From: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: backend: colour-keyed layers start the second pipe

The backend's colour key (0043) acts in alpha blender 1, which mixes the
two pipes: "the layer color key match another channel pixel data in
Alpha Blender1" (F1C200s manual, layer attribute bits 19:18). The atomic
check moved a layer to pipe 1 only when it had alpha, so with opaque
layers everything sat in pipe 0 and a COLOR_KEY property did nothing (seen
on the board through the writeback connector: keyed magenta stayed).

Start the second pipe at a keyed layer, or above the lowest layer when
that one is keyed, and refuse a mix of alpha and keys that would need a
third pipe. Also set the lowest layer's pipe to 0 explicitly.

What a key does, as seen on the board through the writeback connector: a
keyed layer wins wherever the layer in the other pipe has the key colour.
COLOR_KEY on the lower plane makes the key-coloured pixels of the planes
above see-through to it (the classic video-under-UI hole); on the top
plane it changes nothing.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_backend.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_backend.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_backend.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_backend.c
@@ -744,18 +744,35 @@
 	    (plane_states[0]->alpha != DRM_BLEND_ALPHA_OPAQUE))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	state_to_sun4i_layer_state(plane_states[0])->pipe = 0;
 	for (i = 1; i < num_planes; i++) {
 		struct drm_plane_state *p_state = plane_states[i];
 		struct drm_framebuffer *fb = p_state->fb;
 		struct sun4i_layer_state *s_state = state_to_sun4i_layer_state(p_state);
+		bool keyed = s_state->color_key & SUN4I_COLOR_KEY_ENABLE;
+		bool lowest_keyed = i == 1 &&
+			(state_to_sun4i_layer_state(plane_states[0])->color_key &
+			 SUN4I_COLOR_KEY_ENABLE);
 
 		/*
 		 * The only alpha position is the lowest plane of the
 		 * second pipe.
+		 *
+		 * The colour key, too, works only between the two pipes
+		 * (in alpha blender 1: "the layer color key match another
+		 * channel pixel data"), so a keyed layer starts the second
+		 * pipe, or, when the lowest layer is keyed, the layer above
+		 * it does.
 		 */
-		if (fb->format->has_alpha || (p_state->alpha != DRM_BLEND_ALPHA_OPAQUE))
+		if (fb->format->has_alpha || (p_state->alpha != DRM_BLEND_ALPHA_OPAQUE) ||
+		    keyed || lowest_keyed)
 			current_pipe++;
 
+		if (current_pipe > 1) {
+			DRM_DEBUG_DRIVER("Alpha and colour key need more than two pipes\n");
+			return -EINVAL;
+		}
+
 		s_state->pipe = current_pipe;
 	}
 
